(c) may provide for penalties not exceeding a fine of $50,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or both for each offence and, in the case of a continuing offence, a further penalty not exceeding a fine of 10 per cent of the maximum fine prescribed for that offence for every day or part thereof during which the offence continues after conviction. (sections 2 and 37)

